MediaTek connectivity (Wi-Fi + Bluetooth + GNSS + FM) for mainline 7.x, out of tree.

Packaged builds: the linux-cezanne PKGBUILD fetches the vendor repositories
below at pinned commits, copies btif / fmradio from vendor/ (pristine 4.14
BSP sources), applies patches/<name>.patch to each, adds compat/ and
Kbuild.6885, and builds the modules; no local checkout is needed. The
manual steps below are the development setup (src/connectivity working
trees; regenerate patches/ from them after a change).

Sources: github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-<repo>,
branch android-15-release-vvob35 (conninfra, wlan-adaptor, wlan-core-gen4m, common, connfem).
Clone them into src/connectivity/<repo>, apply patches/<repo>.patch, copy compat/,
and symlink the Android layout:
  src/vtop/vendor/mediatek/kernel_modules/connectivity/{conninfra,common,connfem,
    wlan/adaptor -> wlan-adaptor, wlan/core/gen4m -> wlan-core-gen4m}

Build (kernel Module.symvers = vmlinux.symvers, cfg80211 built in):
  build.sh conninfra
  build2.sh wlan-adaptor CONNAC_VER=2_0 MODULE_NAME=wmt_chrdev_wifi_connac2
  build2.sh wlan-core-gen4m SEGMENT=SP MODULE_NAME=wlan_drv_gen4m_6885 \
	KO_CODE_PATH=$HOME/arch-port/src/connectivity/wlan-core-gen4m
Install the stripped .ko into /usr/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/extra, depmod.
Runtime: cezanne-wifi.service (mainline/rootfs). Firmware: MIUI vendor/firmware soc3_0_*.

Bluetooth:
  - btif: the 4.14 BSP BTIF driver (AP <-> CONNSYS serial link), not in the vendor
    repos: copy src/kernel-port/drivers/misc/mediatek/btif/common into
    src/connectivity/btif, apply patches/btif.patch (adds Kbuild + compat_btif.h).
  - bt-mt66xx: vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-bt-mt66xx (same branch),
    apply patches/bt-mt66xx.patch (BlueZ mode: USE_DEVICE_NODE=0, CFG_SUPPORT_BLUEZ,
    late hci registration, set_bdaddr + quirks, connfem stubs).
  - symlinks: src/vtop/.../connectivity/{btif -> btif, bt -> bt-mt66xx}
  Build:
    build.sh btif
    build2.sh bt-mt66xx/6885          (-> bt_drv_6885.ko, needs CONFIG_BT=y)
  Runtime: cezanne-bt.service (after cezanne-wifi). Firmware: soc3_0_ram_{mcu,bt}_1_1_hdr.bin,
  BT_FW.cfg (MIUI vendor/firmware).

GNSS (GPS data link):
  - gps: vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-gps (same branch), apply
    patches/gps.patch (KO_PATH from $(M): 7.x makes $(src) relative; compat include
    as conninfra; void platform remove). MT6885 = data_link/plat/v010 (symlinks into
    data_link/).
  Build:
    build2.sh gps/data_link/plat/v010 CONFIG_MTK_GPS_SUPPORT=y   (-> gps_drv_dl_v010.ko)
  Runtime: cezanne-gps.service (after cezanne-wifi; udev load blacklisted), DT node gps
  + gps-reserve-memory (1 MiB). /dev/gpsdl0 (L1), /dev/gpsdl1 (L5), /dev/gps_emi.
  The DSP needs its RAM code downloaded by the host after open (MIUI: libmnl).
